<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stamp Act 1765</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1765</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Stamp Act of 1765 was a British law requiring printed materials in the American colonies, such as legal documents, newspapers and playing cards, to carry a tax stamp. It was the first direct tax imposed by Parliament on the colonies and provoked riots, boycotts and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stamp-act-congress">Stamp Act Congress</a>, under the slogan of no taxation without representation. Parliament repealed it in 1766 but passed the Declaratory Act asserting its authority.</p></div>
